 describe dense indices with no holes and keep","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their laws. A conformer reports them only while it has no holes of that kind.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Algorithms over the incidence rows use this refinement to number the live vertices and edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with arrays while holes exist, instead of hashing every vertex and edge they meet. The bounds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are upper bounds only. Positions are never reused, so a bound counts every position ever handed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, and nothing in the library allocates by it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In addition to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":"’s laws:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"containsVertex(atPosition: p)"},{"text":" is true exactly for the positions of live vertices, all in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexPositionBound"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexPosition(of:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex(atPosition:)"},{"text":" are inverses, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" lists the live vertices in increasing position. Likewise","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"containsEdge(atPosition:)"},{"text":" is true exactly for the positions in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"text":", all in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgePositionBound"},{"text":", which ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"text":" lists in increasing order.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineCont